From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:05:38 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: open the CC title menu sub lists, configurable title
 entry ids

Generic CC title menu (TitleMenuType.CC: cc, chn, sg-pc profiles):

- Clicking CONTINUE / LOAD or EXTRA only remembered the sub list (the show and hide calls were commented out), so
  the sub entries were never shown and could not be chosen. OpenSubMenu / CloseSubMenu now show the sub list, move
  the focus to its first entry and take it from the main list; Back or choosing a sub entry closes it again and
  gives the focus back to the entry that opened it (the Back press is not passed on to the script). Hiding the
  title also closes an open sub list.
- New optional profile fields: the SW_TITLECUR1 values of the buttons (ConfigId, HelpId, LoadId, QuickLoadId,
  TipsId, LibraryId, EndingListId) and the rows of the two sub lists (ContinueSubRow, ExtraSubRow). The defaults
  are the previous constants, so profiles that do not set them behave as before.
- sg-pc: STEINS;GATE's title script numbers the entries 0 START, 10 QUICK LOAD, 11 LOAD, 20 CLEAR LIST, 21 CG
  LIBRARY, 24 TIPS, 30 CONFIG, 40 HELP (Chaos;Child uses 20 for CONFIG, 10/11 the other way round), so CONFIG used
  to open the clear list and the LOAD entries were swapped. The sub lists now open on the row of their main entry,
  side by side instead of on top of each other.

Checked on MuMu (Android 15): title LOAD shows LOAD / QUICK LOAD, LOAD opens the load screen, Back returns to the
title, loading a slot continues the game; CONFIG and HELP reach their script paths.

